<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>working by hand, practice of a handicraft</i> or <i>art,
				skill herein,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				673
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώμη</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνῶσις</span> (theory), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				259
			</span></i> e; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύνεσις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Amat.</u>
				135b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ahandicraft</i> or <i>art,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				258d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				277c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ζωγράφων . . ἡ καλὴ χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					33.1
				</span></i>
			: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τέχνας ἢ χειρουργίας τινάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					203a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Grg.</u>
				450b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> esp. <i>the
				art</i> or <i>practice of surgery,</i> opp. the
			administration of medicine, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργίῃ
				χρῆσθαι</span> perform <i>an operation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				[23]
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργίην ἐν γραφῇ διηγεῖσθαι</span>”
				<i>the mode of operation,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Art.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.253
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				8.24.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.12
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
